* Ethereum: a gas story
** 2015 Frontier
*** One price list, first-price auction
*** SLOAD 50, new slot 20,000
*** Gas limit 5,000 then 3,141,592
** 2016 Shanghai attacks
*** Cheap state reads, gas limit cut to 500,000
*** EIP-150: repricing, 63/64 rule
*** EIP-160, EIP-161, EIP-170
** 2017-2019
*** REVERT returns unused gas
*** EIP-1283 withdrawn (Petersburg)
*** Istanbul: SLOAD 800, calldata 16
*** EIP-2200: net metering + 2,300 guard
left side
** 2021 Berlin and London
*** Cold / warm access, access lists
*** EIP-1559: base fee burned, target
*** EIP-3529: refunds cut, gas tokens end
** 2022-2024
*** Merge: validators set the limit
*** EIP-4844: blob gas market
*** Transient storage (EIP-1153)
** 2025-2026
*** Gas limit 30M to 60M
*** EIP-7623 calldata floor
*** EIP-7825: cap 16,777,216 per tx
*** Glamsterdam: state gas per byte
